     "result_text_tail": " added revenue that is only delayed to revenue lost for good. The headline and the timing comparison now reflect both.\n\n**Choices I made in place of your answers:**\n- Audience: the CEO and executive team approving or rejecting the launch.\n- Theme: navy.\n- I approved the storyline myself.\n- The 667-request cap is my policy choice: inference may use up to half of the $12 per-seat premium.\n- The six-month checkpoint is 15% of accounts on Pro, half the break-even uptake, assuming upgrades come in evenly over the year.\n- I counted the $0.6M a year platform cost as a cost of revenue.\n\n**Two QA warnings remain, both accepted:**\n- The capped-margin figure on the usage slide isn't computed from that slide's chart. It shows the effect of the fix the chart argues for, so I kept it.\n- The pack says \"two quarters\" in words, so the check can't match the number 2 against the source text.\n\n**Open caveats:**\n- The rewrite's end date on the roadmap slide is illustrative; the pack doesn't give its length.\n- Every result from the beta rests on volunteer accounts, so treat the productivity and renewal gains as a ceiling.\n\nPossible next steps: switch theme (`crimson`, `mono`, `slate`, and others), or add an appendix with the scenario table (uptake of 14%, 33% and 46%).\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `brightwork-copilot.pptx`\n- `brightwork-copilot-sources.xlsx` (one sheet per content slide, with live formulas for every calculated number)\n- `brightwork-copilot.json` (editable source for the deck)"
